    "upgraded-rgba",
    "temporal"
  ],
  "description": "The image seen through glass embossed by its own luminance: luma-gradient normals refract seven wavelength taps whose Cauchy dispersion (scaled by Refraction Depth) is weighted through a per-channel-normalised wavelength-to-RGB response, so bright edges split into spectral fringes while flat grey stays grey. A Laplacian caustic network focuses the pointer light into bright filaments along convex luma crests, with pointer specular, Fresnel rim, subsurface tint and click waves. Depth thickens the glass, with a minimum slab so it works without a depth map.",
